# Deployment safety

| Environment | Convex | Id |
|---|---|---|
| Development | `effervescent-kangaroo-10` | kangaroo |
| Staging | `dapper-roadrunner-247` | roadrunner |
| Production | `tremendous-sturgeon-449` | sturgeon |
| Recovery | `vivid-mosquito-28` | mosquito |

Pages project: `icanova`. Staging: `https://icanova.pages.dev`.

## Staging build (mandatory)

Use **`pnpm build:staging` only** — never bare `pnpm build` for staging. Vite production mode can bake `.env.local` (wrong Convex) into the bundle.

### Before staging deploy

1. Confirm `build:staging` · 2. Target `roadrunner` · 3. Expected Convex URL · 4. Secret scan · 5. Inspect dist (no private creds / no accidental production URL) · 6. Intended commit + clean intent

### After staging deploy

Open live URL → loads → talks to `roadrunner` → auth → key routes → org/device data if present → console/logs → record URL, commit, rollback. Build success ≠ deploy success.

## Production

**Not authorized by default.** Do not deploy/configure/`sturgeon`, migrate prod users, or point Pages at production without explicit owner authorization. Bugfix / “prepare production” / docs edits ≠ prod auth. Keep `mosquito` isolated. Never copy staging secrets into production.
